==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ʌntʃ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# A [[stoop]]ed or [[curl]]ed [[posture]]; a [[slouch]].
#: ''The old man walked with a '''hunch'''.''
# A [[theory]], [[idea]], or [[guess]].
#: ''I have a '''hunch''' they'll find a way to solve the problem.''
# A [[hunk]] (piece of something)

